<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Additives are distinct from fillers (which bulk up volume) and the matrix. They perform specific chemical or physical modifications."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "additive role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance intentionally added in relatively small amounts to modify the processing characteristics, performance properties, or cost of a base material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "UV stabilizers added to dashboard polymers to prevent sun damage; Plasticizers added to PVC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000868> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Organic colorants (dyes) offer high color strength and brightness but may have lower thermal stability than pigments."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organic colorant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A natural organic material used as a colorant in a polymer, coating, or other material system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Azo dyes used in interior textile coloring."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inorganic colorants (pigments) are generally insoluble and provide opacity and high heat stability."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "inorganic colorant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An engineered material used as an inorganic colorant in a polymer, coating, or other material system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Titanium dioxide (white) used in car paints."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000003> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This role can be borne by organic dyes or inorganic pigments."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "colorant role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by an additive substance when its primary function is to impart color to a material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Carbon black acting as a pigment to turn a tire black."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000952> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: MPa."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "For brittle materials, this is equal to tensile strength. For ductile materials, it may be lower than the yield point."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "stress at break"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A strength that quantifies tensile stress at specimen rupture."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A value of 150 MPa for a GF-reinforced polymer."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Can be defined descriptively (Red) or metrologically (L*a*b* coordinates)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "color"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An optical property that characterizes reflected or transmitted light by hue, saturation, and brightness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The 'Piano Black' finish on a B-pillar trim."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050004> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Polyamides are semi-crystalline polymers known for good thermal and chemical resistance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "polyamide"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polymer containing repeating amide (-CONH-) linkages in the polymer backbone."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Nylon 6, Nylon 12, Nylon 66."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "PA" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000009> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "PA66 has a higher melting point around 260 degC than PA6 but absorbs moisture, which affects dimensional stability."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "polyamide 66"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "PA66"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A semicrystalline thermoplastic polyamide synthesized from hexamethylenediamine and adipic acid."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Material used for cylinder head covers and radiator end tanks."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000010> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "PA66" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The addition of 25% glass fiber significantly increases stiffness and tensile strength compared to neat PA66."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "polyamide 66 glass fiber 25 percent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "PA66-GF25"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A composite material that has a polyamide 66 matrix and nominally 25 percent glass fiber by mass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Structural components in the engine bay requiring high stiffness at elevated temperatures."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In PMD logic, this is a disconnected aggregate because the individual filaments in a bundle are distinct objects."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fiber"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disconnected material entity aggregate composed of elongated filament-like material parts."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Carbon fiber tow, Aramid fibers."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000012> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Used extensively as a reinforcement agent in polymer matrix composites."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "glass fiber"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fiber composed primarily of glass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "E-Glass used to reinforce PA66 for automotive pedals."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000013> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "GF" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Commonly denoted as wt%. PA66-GF25 implies a value of 0.25 or 25%."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: %."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fiber material content mass fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mass proportion that quantifies fiber reinforcement mass relative to total composite material mass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "25% mass fraction in PA66-GF25."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: %."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Volume fraction is more critical for micromechanical modeling (e.g., Rule of Mixtures) than mass fraction."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fiber material content volume fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "volume fraction of fibers"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A volume proportion that quantifies fiber reinforcement volume relative to total composite material volume."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Approximately 14-15% volume fraction corresponds to 25% mass fraction for Glass/PA66."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identifier at manufacturer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier assigned by a manufacturer to a product, component, material grade, or material batch in its own system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A manufacturer code for a specific polymer grade."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identifier name at manufacturer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records the manufacturer name, brand name, or trade name used for a material or product."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Zytel or Durethan used as a material trade name."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material designation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records a standard or supplier designation for a material composition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000018> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "PA66-GF25"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material identifier"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier assigned to a material entity, material batch, material grade, or material data record."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A material twin identifier used in data exchange."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/log/LOG_0080002> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material batch identifier"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A batch identifier assigned to a material batch for traceability."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Batch 2023-10-A-X55."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:string; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "business partner number"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier assigned to a business partner in an automotive supply-chain network."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "BPNL00000003AY2 (Example BPN)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000021> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "BPN" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: not specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates ductility. Low strain at break (less than 5%) suggests brittle behavior."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "strain at break"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mechanical property that quantifies specimen strain at rupture."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "3% strain at break for a glass-filled polyamide."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: Pa.s."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Used in injection molding simulations to predict mold filling."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An intensive quality that quantifies a fluid material's resistance to flow."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The melt viscosity of polypropylene at 230 degC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: Pa.s."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Polymers are non-Newtonian; their shear viscosity decreases as shear rate increases (shear thinning)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "shear viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A viscosity that quantifies resistance to flow under shear deformation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Viscosity curve data required for Moldflow simulation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000882> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Below Tg, the amorphous phase is frozen; above Tg, polymer chains have mobility."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: degC."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "glass transition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A phase boundary temperature at which the amorphous phase of a polymer changes between glassy and rubbery states."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A glass transition temperature of about 50 degC for dry PA66."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000026> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "Tg" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000981> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: 1/K."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Used to calculate dimensional change in assemblies that combine materials with different thermal expansion behavior."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coefficient of linear thermal expansion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "linear thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thermal property that quantifies fractional length change per unit temperature change."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "CLTE measured parallel and normal to fiber orientation in a reinforced polymer part."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000027> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "CLTE" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: J kg^-1 K^-1."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Used to calculate cooling times in injection molding."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "specific heat capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A heat capacity that quantifies heat required to raise the temperature of unit mass of a substance by one temperature unit."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A specific heat capacity of 1700 J kg^-1 K^-1 for polypropylene."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000028> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050117> "Cp" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000952> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kJ/m^2."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Often measured via Charpy or Izod notched impact tests."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "impact strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A strength that quantifies material resistance to fracture under impact loading."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "45 kJ/m^2 notched impact strength for a bumper material."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000949> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: MPa / GPa."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Standard metric for stiffness in plastics (ISO 178)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "flexural modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stiffness that quantifies the ratio of flexural stress to flexural strain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Flexural modulus of 8500 MPa for PA66-GF30."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000952> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: MPa / GPa."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relevant for snap-fit joints in automotive interiors."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "flexural strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A strength that quantifies maximum stress under flexural loading before yielding or rupture."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "250 MPa for a high-performance composite."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relevant for polyamides because moisture uptake changes mechanical properties."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "humidity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An intensive quality that quantifies water vapor content in air surrounding a material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0000032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "50% Relative Humidity (standard conditioning atmosphere)."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/log/LOG_1000102> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether a material is raw material depends on its participation in a particular production or recycling workflow."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "raw material feedstock"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material entity that is intended to be consumed, transformed, or incorporated as input in a manufacturing, recycling, or material processing process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010000> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "PA66 pellets supplied to an injection molding process as input material."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class represents the additive material itself; the context-dependent function is represented by additive role."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "additive"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An engineered material intentionally incorporated in a base material in a comparatively small amount to modify processing behavior, performance properties, appearance, or cost."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A UV stabilizer added to an exterior polymer trim material."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The corresponding realizable entity is PMD Core matrix role; this class is used for material entities considered as the continuous phase of a composite."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "matrix"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An engineered material that forms the continuous phase of a composite material and binds or embeds reinforcement, filler, or dispersed material constituents."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The PA66 phase in a PA66-GF25 composite."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: %."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Values are normally reported for specified test conditions, such as ISO 62 or a specified conditioning atmosphere."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "water absorption"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a material to take up water from a liquid water or humid environment under specified exposure conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The percentage mass increase of a polyamide specimen after immersion in water."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "materials information"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "material data"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "material information"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information content entity that specifies material-related characteristics of a product, component, material batch, or material grade."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A data record listing material designation, density, fiber content, and recycled content for an automotive component."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material composition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "materials"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A composition that describes the material constituents and constituent amounts of a product, component, material batch, or material grade."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A composition stating that PA66-GF25 contains a PA66 matrix and nominally 25 percent glass fiber by mass."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class covers material entities whose origin is a recycling process; the amount or share of recycled content should be represented separately."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycled material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material entity that has been recovered from waste, discarded products, by-products, or production residues through a recycling process for subsequent use."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Regranulated polypropylene produced from end-of-life vehicle parts."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use for the origin state of a material; use recycled material share for quantities or proportions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycled"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a material entity indicating that the material has an origin in a recycling process rather than only in primary material production."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A recycled quality borne by a polymer regrind used in a new injection molding batch."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "product footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information content entity that records an environmental footprint of a product over a stated scope."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A product footprint report for an alternator covering cradle-to-gate carbon emissions and recycled material content."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycled material share"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "recycled share"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A relational quality that relates a material, component, or product to the proportion of its material content that originates from recycled sources."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010021> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A bumper fascia with 30 percent recycled polypropylene content."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010020> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kg CO2e."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "product carbon footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "carbon footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "carbon footprint amount"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A product footprint that specifies greenhouse gas emissions associated with a product over a stated lifecycle scope."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010022> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "18.4 kg CO2e as the product carbon footprint for one steering system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "process footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process attribute that quantifies environmental burden associated with executing a process under specified boundary conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Electricity consumption and associated emissions for one injection molding cycle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "process carbon footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process footprint that quantifies greenhouse gas emissions associated with executing a process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The carbon footprint of recycling one kilogram of PA66-GF25 scrap."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "lifecycle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process chain that comprises the stages through which a product or material passes from raw material acquisition through production, use, and end-of-life treatment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The lifecycle of an automotive control unit from material extraction to recycling."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "lifecycle stage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "footprint lifecycle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process that is a distinguishable part of a product or material lifecycle."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Main product production as a lifecycle stage for an automotive component."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "raw material acquisition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lifecycle stage in which natural resources, secondary materials, or basic feedstocks are obtained and prepared for production."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Obtaining recycled polymer regranulate for later component production."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "main product production"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lifecycle stage in which raw materials, intermediate products, or components are transformed into the main product."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010028> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Injection molding and assembly steps used to produce an automotive housing."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "distribution"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lifecycle stage in which products, components, or materials are transported, stored, or transferred between supply chain actors."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Shipment of remanufactured components from a supplier to a vehicle manufacturer."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "end of life"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lifecycle stage in which a product or component has reached the end of its intended use and is directed to reuse, remanufacturing, recycling, recovery, or disposal."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Removal of a component from an end-of-life vehicle for circular value assessment."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010026> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycling lifecycle stage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "recycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lifecycle stage in which used materials or products are processed to recover material for further use."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Grinding, sorting, and regranulating a polymer component after dismantling."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kg CO2e."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycling carbon footprint estimate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "footprint recycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A product carbon footprint estimate that specifies greenhouse gas emissions for a recycling scenario."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "12 kg CO2e attributed to recycling one dismantled bumper cover."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kg CO2e."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remanufacturing carbon footprint estimate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "footprint remanufacturing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A product carbon footprint estimate that specifies greenhouse gas emissions for a remanufacturing scenario."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "7.5 kg CO2e attributed to inspecting, repairing, and remanufacturing one alternator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kg CO2e."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reuse carbon footprint estimate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "footprint reuse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An estimated product carbon footprint value that specifies greenhouse gas emissions for a reuse scenario."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "2.1 kg CO2e attributed to checking and reusing one component."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: kg CO2e."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "new production carbon footprint estimate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "footprint new production"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A product carbon footprint estimate that specifies greenhouse gas emissions for a new production scenario."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "24 kg CO2e attributed to manufacturing one replacement component from primary material."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Expected value datatype: xsd:float; expected unit: %."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "humidity absorption"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a material or component to absorb water vapor from a humid environment under specified exposure conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Moisture uptake by a PA66 component during use at 50 percent relative humidity."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000202> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remaining lifetime"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal interval expected to remain before a product or component no longer satisfies its intended function or circular value criteria."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010050> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An alternator estimated to have 24 months of usable service life remaining after inspection."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000202> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "actual lifetime"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal interval extending from a stated start event to an observed lifecycle event of a product or component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010051> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The time between first vehicle registration and dismantling of a component."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "non-destructive dismantlability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product or component to be dismantled without destroying the product, component, or material portions that are intended for later use."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010052> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A clipped interior trim part that can be removed intact for reuse."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "safety information"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "safetyInfo"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A directive information entity that specifies safety-relevant instructions, warnings, or constraints for handling, dismantling, treating, transporting, or reusing a product or component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010053> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A warning to disconnect a high-voltage battery before dismantling a component."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process in which used materials, components, or products are collected and processed to recover material for further use."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010054> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Sorting and regranulating polymer parts from an end-of-life vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dismantling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process in which a product or component is taken apart so that parts, materials, or information can be recovered, assessed, reused, repaired, remanufactured, recycled, or disposed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Removing a vehicle door module from an end-of-life vehicle before quality assessment."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dismantling guideline for recycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dismantling guideline recycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dismantlingGuidelineRecycling"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan specification that provides instructions for dismantling a product or component so that materials can be routed to appropriate recycling treatment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A guideline specifying how to separate a polymer housing from attached metal inserts before recycling."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycling material quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "recyclingMaterialQuality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product or material to be recycled while preserving a specified level of material quality."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A polymer component designed so that the recovered polymer remains suitable for automotive applications."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recycling availability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "recyclingAvailability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product, component, or material to be practically available for recycling in a technical cycle."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010058> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A component whose material can be separated and accepted by an established recycling route."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dismantling instructions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dismantlingInstructions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan specification that describes the actions, order, tools, and constraints for safely and correctly dismantling a product or component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010059> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Stepwise instructions for removing a battery module from a vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dismantlability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product or component to be dismantled under stated technical, safety, time, and damage constraints."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010060> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A bolted assembly has higher dismantlability than an inseparably bonded assembly when reuse is intended."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000202> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "average dismantling time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "averageDismantlingTime"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal interval that represents the mean duration of dismantling a product or component under specified conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An average dismantling time of 12 minutes for removal of a door module."@en .
