<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010068> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An exploded-view diagram showing screws, clips, housing shells, and subcomponents of a control unit."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sub-group name"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records the name of a material sub-group in a material classification scheme."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010069> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The VDA 231-106 sub-group name 'cast aluminium alloys'."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sub-group identifier"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "sub-group ID"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "subgroup"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records the code or number of a material sub-group in a material classification scheme."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The VDA 231-106 sub-group code '2.1.1'."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "main group name"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records the name of a material main group in a material classification scheme."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The VDA 231-106 main group name 'polymer materials'."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "main group identifier"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "main group"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "main group ID"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier that records the code or number of a material main group in a material classification scheme."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The VDA 231-106 main group code '5'."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reuse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process in which a discarded or removed product or component is used again while retaining its original function."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010073> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A dismantled and inspected body control module installed in another vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "product quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product or component to satisfy requirements for an intended circular economy route, based on relevant condition, completeness, functional, and standard-based criteria."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010074> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A reused body part assigned a quality class after inspection for dents, corrosion, paint damage, and completeness."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "test requirements"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "necessary test protocols and equipment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "necessary test protocols equipment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information content entity that states the test protocols and equipment required to assess a product or component for reuse, repair, remanufacturing, or recycling."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A high-voltage component requiring insulation resistance testing before reuse."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reusability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A disposition of a product or component to be reused in its original function under stated technical, legal, safety, and quality constraints."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A complete undamaged headlamp assembly that can be installed as a replacement part."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "body part quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "component quality state"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "quality body parts"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a body part component that characterizes its externally relevant condition, such as paint damage, dents, corrosion, and component-specific defects."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A door panel quality assessment based on dents and paint scratches."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "quality grade"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "qualityGrade"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality that records the grade assigned to a product or component according to a stated quality standard or assessment scheme."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A, B, or C quality grade assigned to a used car part."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "completeness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a product or component indicating whether required subcomponents, fasteners, interfaces, or accessories are present."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010079> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A mirror assembly assessed as complete because housing, glass, wiring, and mounting clips are present."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "used quality standard"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "usedQualityStandard"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan specification that defines the quality assessment criteria applied to a reused, repaired, remanufactured, or recycled product or component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "VDI 4080 used as the assessment standard for reuse quality."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mounting point integrity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "mountingPointIntegrity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a product or component indicating whether its mounting points, clips, tabs, or attachment features are intact and functional."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A bumper bracket with all mounting tabs undamaged."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "surface cleanliness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "surfaceCleanliness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a product, component, or material surface indicating the degree to which it is free from oil, dust, residues, and other contaminants."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010082> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A cleaned polymer surface acceptable for adhesive bonding during reuse preparation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000202> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "repair time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "repairTime"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal interval required or estimated to repair a specified damage or defect on a product or component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010083> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The time needed to repair a paint scratch and small dent on a door panel."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "crack count"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "(number of paint) cracks"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "cracks"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality that records the number of cracks observed on a product, component, coating, or material surface."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010084> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Two cracks recorded in the paint layer during dismantling inspection."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dent damage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dents"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a sheet metal or body component indicating the presence or extent of dents or deformations that impair the component shape."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010085> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A quarter panel with two visible dents after vehicle use."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "damage area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "damageArea"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality that quantifies the surface area of visible damage on a product, component, coating, or material surface."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010086> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A paint damage area of 50 square centimeters on a door panel."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "paint damage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "paintDamage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of a painted product or component indicating damage to the paintwork, such as scratches, chips, cracks, or coating loss."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010087> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Stone-chip damage on a painted bumper cover."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010090
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010090> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010090> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000> .
