# https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "environmental condition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality of an environment that is relevant to material behavior, processing, testing, storage, use, or degradation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/AUTOMATCE_0010100> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A conditioning atmosphere with specified temperature and relative humidity."@en .
