<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "See the editor note of composition to understand the difference between composition and chemical composition.\n\nSee the pattern example of composition to underatand the difference between composition and proportion."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemical composition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemische Zusammensetzung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die chemische Zusammensetzung ist eine intensive Eigenschaft eines Materieteils, die die Arten und Anteile reiner chemischer Elemente in dem Materieteil beschreibt, und ist Gegenstand einiger Datenelemente zur chemischen Zusammensetzung."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The chemical composition is an intensive quality of a portion of matter which describes the types and proportions of pure chemical elements in the portion of matter, and it is a subject of some chemical composition data item."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemical potential"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemisches Potential"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "a quality of a thermodynamic system describing the energy change associated with the addition of a small quantity of a substance to a system at constant temperature and pressure."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "eine intensive Qualität eines thermodynamischen Systems, die die Energieänderung beschreibt, die mit der Zugabe einer kleinen Menge einer Substanz zu einem System bei konstanter Temperatur und konstantem Druck verbunden ist."@de .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000890> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "composite"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An object aggregate that consists of two or more bonded materials with dissimilar physical or chemical properties which are used to complement each other where the parts remain seperate and distinct in the resulting object aggregate."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "carbon fibre reinforced polymer\nlaminated glass\nwood\nhard metal composites for abrasive tools" .
