<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000868> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "natural organic material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000868> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "material derived from natural biological sources or processes"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemical reaction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chemische Reaktion"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Das Auftreten einer chemischen Reaktion ist der Prozess, bei dem Substanzen interagieren, um neue chemische Verbindungen zu bilden oder ihre Molekülstruktur zu verändern."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The occurrence of (a) chemical reaction is the process in which substances interact to form new chemical compounds or alter their molecular structure."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020265> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optical property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optische Eigenschaft"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "a property that is commonly associated with the domain of optics"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A camera lens has an optical capability of resolving 100 line pairs per mm at the image plane"@en .
