<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Concentrations can be expressed in terms of three quantifiers:\n\n+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+\n---------------------+\n|                   | count            | mass              | volume              |\n length                  |  area\n+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+\n| per count         | molar fraction  | -------  |-------  |\n ------ | ------\n| per mass          | count per mass   | mass per mass     | volume per mass     |\n ------- | ---------\n| per volume        | count per volume | mass per volume   | volume per volume   |\n| per length         | length number density  |-------  | ------ | length fraction | --------\n| per area          |  area number density  |-------  | ------ | -------- | area fraction\n+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+\n\nMass per count and volume per count are not known to have practical examples but are included for completeness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kamilla:\n1.  concentration is a bad name, cause area fraction (texture component or phase on the image) is also relationship between part and the whole.\n2. Number desity (of precipitates) can be the same as count per volume or count per area or count per length. How to deal with that?"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ratio: \nA comparison of two or more quantities (a relationship), e.g. 3:2:1 for prosecco, aperol and sparkling water in aperol spritz. There is no stanardized mathematical notation or operators for it.  We do not support it, rather convert it to fractions.\n\nProportion: \nA statement that two ratios/fractions are equal (an equation), e.g. 2/3=4/6"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fraction property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "part-whole property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "a property describing a quantitative relation between two entites where one entity represents the whole and the other entity represents a part of the whole"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "aperol spritz: 3/6 prosecco, 2/6 aperol, 1/6 sparkling water in vol/vol"@en .
