_:genid766 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> .
_:genid766 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020161> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "activity (thermodynamic)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020161> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermodynamische Aktivität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020161> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermodynamic activity is a relational quality that inheres between a chemical species and a non-ideal solution and represents the effective concentration of the species accounting for particle interactions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020161> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermodynamische Aktivität ist eine Beziehungsqualität, die zwischen einer chemischen Spezies und einer nicht idealen Lösung innewohnt und die effektive Konzentration der Spezies darstellt, die für Partikelwechselwirkungen verantwortlich ist."@de .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aktivierungsenergie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "activation energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020162> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Activation energy (E_a) a process attribute characterizing the minimum amount of energy required to initiate a reaction, allowing educts to overcome an energy barrier to transform into products."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000882> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Zustandsgrenze der Materie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "state of matter boundary"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A state of matter boundary is a phase boundary that is realized by the transition from one aggregate state to another aggregate state."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eine Zustandsgrenze ist eine Phasengrenze, die durch den Übergang von einem Aggregatzustand in einen anderen Aggregatzustand realisiert wird."@de .
